### MemberCreateRequest validation examples
### The project currently has no member controller. These requests become executable
### after a POST endpoint accepts MemberCreateRequest with @Valid.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@memberEndpoint = {{baseUrl}}/api/members

### Valid member request (expected: successful response after endpoint implementation)
POST {{memberEndpoint}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "홍길동",
  "email": "member@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Blank name (expected: 400, name validation error)
POST {{memberEndpoint}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "email": "member@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Invalid email format (expected: 400, email validation error)
POST {{memberEndpoint}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "홍길동",
  "email": "wrong-email",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Password shorter than 8 characters (expected: 400, password validation error)
POST {{memberEndpoint}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "홍길동",
  "email": "member@example.com",
  "password": "1234567"
}
